<div style="border: 2px solid #1a5276; padding: 15px; text-align: center; background-color: #e0f2f7;">
    <h1 style="color: #1a5276; margin: 0; font-size: 2em;">Lesson Planner – Theme # <span style="color: #000;">How I Am Successful</span> – Lesson # 4</h1>
    <p style="color: #1a5276; margin: 5px 0 0 0; font-size: 1.2em;"><em>Complete this planner five times per theme, once per lesson (Lesson 1 through Lesson 5).</em></p>
</div>

<table style="border: 1px dashed #333; border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%; margin: 10px 0;">
    <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; width: 50%;"><b>Lesson #:</b> 4</td>
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; width: 50%;"><b>Skills Focus:</b> Writing</td>
    </tr>
    <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b>Grade:</b> 12th Grade (CEFR: B1.3)</td>
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b>Scenario:</b> My Personal Success Story</td>
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b>Theme:</b> How I Am Successful</td>
    </tr>
    <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b>Date(s):</b> From ___ to ___</td>
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;" colspan="2"><b>Learning Sequence Time:</b> 45–50 min</td>
    </tr>
    <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;" colspan="3">
            <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Specific Objective:</b> Writing: Productive: Write reflective essays on personal experiences. Interactive: Exchange essays for peer review on common themes.</p>
            <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Learning Outcome:</b> Writing: Can exchange essays with classmates for feedback on personal themes (e.g., "In Amelia's essay, she described overcoming challenges, and I suggested improving the clarity of her conclusion.")
            Can write a reflective essay on a significant learning experience, relating it to future aspirations (e.g., "Working at the local youth center has taught me leadership skills. If I continue mentoring students, I will build connections that could support my future career in social work.")
            Can provide constructive peer feedback in written form (e.g., "Your essay is well organized, but I think you could improve the introduction by adding more context.")</p>
        </td>
    </tr>
</table>

<h2 style="color: #1a5276;">The Six Action-Oriented Approach (AOA) Lesson Stages</h2>
<table style="border: 1px dashed #333; border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%; margin: 10px 0;">
    <thead>
        <tr style="background-color: #e0f2f7;">
            <th style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; width: 33%; color: #1a5276;">Stage & Description</th>
            <th style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; width: 33%; color: #1a5276;">Activities & Teacher Actions</th>
            <th style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; width: 34%; color: #1a5276;">Estimated Date and Time</th>
        </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>STAGE 1 — Warm-up / Pre-task</b></p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Engagement, Modeling and Clarification</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Warm-up:</b> Students individually brainstorm a significant personal **achievement** or **learning experience** that has contributed to their **growth**. They write down 3-5 keywords or phrases related to this experience. Then, in pairs, they share one keyword/phrase and briefly explain its **impact** in one sentence. The teacher ensures students use target vocabulary like 'achievements', 'growth', 'impact', 'personal', 'significant'.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Modeling:</b> The teacher projects a simple sentence: "I have **volunteered** at the local **community service** center, and it has taught me leadership skills." The teacher orally models the sentence, exaggerating the stress on content words (**volunteered**, **community service**, TAUGHT, LEADERSHIP SKILLS) and reducing stress on function words, explaining how this makes the sentence sound more natural. The teacher also shows a brief written outline of a reflective essay (Introduction, Body, Conclusion) on the board and models writing a thesis statement for an essay about volunteering, relating it to future aspirations: "My experience in **community service** has been **essential** for my **personal growth**, shaping my **future** **career** **goals**."</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Clarification (CCQs):</b></p>
                <ul>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"What is the main purpose of a reflective essay?" (Expected: To share a personal experience and what was learned.)</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"Which parts of the essay outline describe what happened, and which part summarizes the learning?" (Expected: Body paragraphs describe, conclusion summarizes learning and future aspirations.)</li>
                </ul>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: center; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">5-7 min</p>
            </td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>STAGE 2 — Presentation</b></p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Input of new language/content connected to Scenario: "My Personal Success Story".</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Material:</b> A short reflective essay excerpt (2-3 paragraphs, 150-200 words) from a 12th-grade student on a personal **success** story related to **achievements** and **future aspirations**. The genre is a narrative essay, reflective register, academic-appropriate format. The text will incorporate target grammar (Present perfect, Future continuous, First conditional) and vocabulary.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Communicative Competence:</b> Writing: Using appropriate structure and language to convey personal reflections and future goals effectively in written form.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Comprehension tasks:</b> Students read the essay excerpt silently. Then, they answer the following questions in their notebooks:</p>
                <ul>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Gist question:</b> What is the main **achievement** the writer is reflecting on?</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>True/False:</b> Read the following statements and indicate if they are True or False according to the text.
                        <ul style="list-style-type: lower-alpha; margin-top: 5px;">
                            <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">The writer has only recently started thinking about their **career** **goals**.</li>
                            <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">The writer believes if they **continue** to **invest** in their **training**, they will **succeed**.</li>
                        </ul>
                    </li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Information matching:</b> Match the verbs from the text (e.g., 'have **managed**', 'will be **pursuing**', 'if I **participate**') to the type of success/goal they describe (e.g., past **achievement**, long-term **future** **goal**, conditional **opportunity**).</li>
                </ul>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: center; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">10 min</p>
            </td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>STAGE 3 — Preparation / Practice</b></p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Accuracy focus on Writing.</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Communicative Skill & Content:</b> Students will practice writing sentences and short paragraphs using Present perfect for **achievements**, Future continuous for long-term **goals**, and First conditional for **future success**, incorporating target vocabulary related to **finances**, **career**, and **personal growth**.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Detailed Procedure:</b></p>
                <ol>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Controlled Practice - Sentence Completion:</b> Students complete sentences using the correct form of the verb (present perfect, future continuous, first conditional) and a suitable vocabulary word from the provided list (e.g., **savings, investment, community service, manage, complete, aspire**).
                        <ul style="list-style-type: disc; margin-top: 5px;">
                            <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">I _______ (save) some money for my college studies. (I have **saved** some money for my college studies.)</li>
                            <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">In five years, I _______ (manage) my own **organization**. (In five years, I **will be managing** my own **organization**.)</li>
                            <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">If I _______ (continue) my **training**, I _______ (find) more **opportunities**. (If I **continue** my **training**, I **will find** more **opportunities**.)</li>
                        </ul>
                    </li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Semi-controlled Practice - Paragraph Expansion:</b> Students work in pairs. Each pair receives three sentence starters related to **personal growth**, **achievements**, and **future goals**. They must expand each starter into a 2-3 sentence paragraph, using target grammar and vocabulary.
                        <ul style="list-style-type: disc; margin-top: 5px;">
                            <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Sentence Starter 1: "Throughout my high school years, I have..." (e.g., I have **participated** in several **projects** and **built** a strong **network**.)</li>
                            <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Sentence Starter 2: "Looking ahead, by the time I am 25, I will be..." (e.g., ...I **will be pursuing** a **professional career** and **managing** my **finances** carefully.)</li>
                            <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Sentence Starter 3: "If I **invest** time in developing new skills..." (e.g., ...I **will broaden** my **opportunities** and **achieve** significant **growth**.)</li>
                        </ul>
                    </li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Peer Check/Review:</b> Pairs exchange their expanded paragraphs with another pair. They check for correct grammar usage (present perfect, future continuous, first conditional) and appropriate vocabulary, providing written suggestions for improvement. Sociolinguistic competence: respectfully discussing achievements and providing constructive feedback.</li>
                </ol>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: center; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">15 min</p>
            </td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>STAGE 4 — Performance / Production</b></p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Communicative task where students USE the language in a realistic scenario: "My Personal Success Story".</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Communicative Task: Reflective Essay Draft</b></p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Students will write a first draft of a reflective essay (approx. 150-200 words) titled "My Personal Success Story". The essay should describe a **significant learning experience** or **achievement**, reflecting on its **impact** on their **personal growth**, and relating it to their **future aspirations**. They must include examples of **present perfect** to discuss past **achievements**, **future continuous** to describe long-term **goals**, and the **first conditional** to discuss **future success** or **opportunities**. Students should aim to use at least 8-10 target vocabulary words from the provided list (e.g., **community service, initiative, investment, career, manage, achieve, aspire, positive, long-term, impact**). They are encouraged to focus on content words and express their ideas clearly.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Task Format:</b> Individual written product (reflective essay draft).</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Connection to Theme/Scenario:</b> The essay directly addresses "How I Am Successful" by focusing on a personal experience and "My Personal Success Story" by requiring students to reflect on their own journey and future. This task emphasizes fluency in expressing personal ideas in written form, using learned grammatical structures and vocabulary.</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: center; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">10 min (In-class draft) + Homework</p>
            </td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>STAGE 5 — Assessment / Post-task</b></p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Formative assessment strategy.</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Formative Assessment Strategy: Peer Feedback and Teacher Observation.</b></p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Assessment Task:</b> Students will exchange their reflective essay drafts with a partner. Each student will read their partner's essay and provide constructive written feedback using a simple peer review checklist focusing on clarity, use of target language, and overall message. They should provide at least two positive comments and one suggestion for improvement.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Evaluation Criteria (Peer Review & Teacher Observation):</b></p>
                <ul>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Content Clarity:</b> Is the main **achievement** or **learning experience** clear? Is its **impact** understandable?</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Use of Target Grammar:</b> Appropriate use of Present Perfect, Future Continuous, and First Conditional (e.g., "If you **continue** to use more future continuous verbs for your long-term **goals**, your essay will flow better.").</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Use of Target Vocabulary:</b> Integration of at least 5 relevant vocabulary words (e.g., "Your choice of 'initiative' to describe your project was very effective.").</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Organization:</b> Clear introduction, body, and conclusion.</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Constructive Feedback (for peer review):</b> Ability to provide helpful, respectful written suggestions.</li>
                </ul>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Student Self-Assessment / Exit Ticket:</b> Students complete an exit ticket after receiving peer feedback:</p>
                <ul>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"One thing I learned about writing a reflective essay today is..."</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"I will **improve** my essay by focusing on..." (e.g., "I will **improve** my essay by focusing on adding more details about how my **community service** experience helped me **achieve** **personal growth**.")</li>
                </ul>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: center; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">10 min</p>
            </td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>STAGE 6 — Reflection</b></p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Student Self-Reflection Prompt:</b></p>
                <ul>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">What was the most challenging part of writing your personal success story? How did you try to overcome it?</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">How has reflecting on your past **achievements** and **future goals** helped you **understand** your aspirations better?</li>
                </ul>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Teacher Reflection:</b></p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">What worked well in this lesson, particularly regarding the writing focus and target grammar/vocabulary? (e.g., "The peer review session was highly effective in encouraging students to apply the feedback criteria and revise their work. Students successfully used the present perfect for achievements.")</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">What adjustments or additional scaffolds might be needed for the next lesson to support students' writing skills further? (e.g., "Some students struggled with consistently using the future continuous. For the next lesson, I will provide more guided practice with sentence frames for describing long-term goals and a quick review of future tenses.")</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Connection to next lesson:</b> In Lesson 5 (Mediation & Integration), students will finalize their reflective essays, possibly turning them into a short presentation or a digital storytelling project, summarizing and integrating the written ideas into a communicative product, demonstrating their **21st Century Skills** project.</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: center; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">5 min</p>
            </td>
        </tr>
    </tbody>
</table>